{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they ceased</b> — Two times in the Masorah: ויחדלו הקולות, ויחדלו לבנות העיר. Teaches that also in the generation of the dispersion HaShem confused them with sounds (קולות) and mixed them up until they ceased building, and also here they ceased building by means of the sounds that went out from under the burdens of Egypt." "<b>He poured</b> — Three times: לא נתך ארצה, עד נתך מים עליהם (regarding the sons of Saul who were impaled), כאשר נתך אפי וחמתי על יושבי ירושלם. To teach that the prayer of the righteous withholds rain, as here regarding Moses; and the prayer of the righteous brings it down, as regarding David, who executed judgment upon the sons of Saul and prayed to HaShem and atoned for them; and so HaShem will atone for Jerusalem through the prayer of the righteous, as written: וכפר אדמתו עמו."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:23.946978311Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}